{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass at the end, etc.</b> The verse does not state what happened, and if it intends the Exodus, behold it goes back and says a second time, ״וַיְהִי בְּעֶצֶם״. Further, one needs to know what sorrow the word <b>וַיְהִי</b> alludes to." "Or perhaps the verse declares the sorrow of their being held back until the appointed end, and they had no merit to leave before the appointed end. Or it may allude that the sorrow that Israel endured during the span mentioned above, as it is written: ״וּמוֹשַׁב בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ etc. (Exodus 12:40), was not for that entire time but only מִקֵּץ, 'from the end.'" "<b>And it came to pass at the very end.</b> It alludes to the sorrow of the departure of those who went out with them, for through them evils were occasioned. Or it may allude that the plagues and troubles did not cease from Egypt even on the very day itself, and so it says (Numbers 33:4): ״וּמִצְרַיִם מְקַבְּרִים״ etc., ״וּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל יוֹצְאִים בְּיָד רָמָה״ (Exodus 14:8)."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:20.874239147Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}